{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nAudit how the artifact-specific concision guidance recorded by inanimate-unrideable-wasp maps to documentation and durable records in the current rebar project.\n\n## Approach\n- Read the canonical documentation policy and indexes, then inspect representative examples of agent guidance, executable-plan guidance, ADRs, user-facing guides, generated reference/API documentation, incident/security material, templates/prompts, ticket comments, and session logs.\n- For each artifact class, compare its stated purpose and observed structure with the proposed contract: minimum sufficient content, progressive disclosure, protected facts, current-versus-historical state, alternatives, evidence, and resumption information.\n- Classify each class as typically following, partially following, or intentionally not following the guidance. Describe concrete deviations and whether they are defects or purpose-driven exceptions.\n- Cite exact repository files and use the existing historical-ticket calibration for tracker artifacts.\n\n## Artifacts\n- A concise answer with repository citations.\n- A ticket comment recording the audit result.\n- No repository files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The answer covers canonical agent guidance, executable tickets/plans, comments/handoffs, ADRs, user-facing documentation, reference/API documentation, incident/security records, and session logs/research notes.\n- [x] Each artifact class has a follows/partially follows/does-not-follow classification.\n- [x] Each non-following or partial class names the specific ways it diverges.\n- [x] Purpose-driven exceptions are distinguished from bloat defects.\n- [x] Claims about repository documentation cite current files.\n- [x] No repository files are modified.\n\n## Verification\nCross-check classifications against docs/documentation-policy.md, docs/README.md, representative files from each artifact class, and the completed 20-ticket calibration."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788499812923586628,"uuid":"839b74ec-1dd4-4fb7-8afc-0896dc9f0ad9"}